      "statement": "Partial article-level comparison verified from e-Gov evidence: National Health Insurance Enforcement Regulation Art. 27-12-2 changes the cross-reference for persons deemed to have received municipal/association recognition from Enforcement Order Art. 29-3(4)(1) or (2) to (1) or (10). Art. 26-6-4 changes the cited Art. 29-3(1)(5) to (13). These are verified cross-reference changes, not proof that eligibility or benefit amounts changed. The complete substantive effects across the three insurance schemes and both commencement stages remain UNCONFIRMED; do not publish based on these excerpts. Further 2027-08-01 stage evidence: National Health Insurance Enforcement Regulation Art. 26-2 (meal-cost standard copayment reduction) changes cross-references to Health Insurance Enforcement Order Art. 43(1)(1) from ホ to ワ and to National Health Insurance Enforcement Order Art. 29-3(1) from item 5 to item 13, alongside other kana renumbering. The evidence pack classifies this as a non-citation-only article change; that classification alone does not establish substantive entitlement expansion or contraction. Full provisions and underlying orders must be compared before concluding legal effects.",
